cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Cycle Time versus Accuracy: Simulation and Economic Model of AI-Based Phenotyping in Smallholder Bean Breeding"
abstract: >-
  Code and data for a coupled breeding-simulation and economic model that values a
  smartphone computer-vision phenotyping tool in a four-stage East African common-bean
  breeding pipeline. Layer 1 is an AlphaSimR stochastic simulation over a factorial grid
  of tool profiles; Layer 2 converts simulated genetic gain into adoption, net present
  value, global sensitivity and value-of-information analyses. Includes the
  meta-analysis extraction sheets and the scripts that generate every number, table and
  figure in the manuscript.
